v0.7:
	firmware beta.6 auto-ranging: publish /Boardstrom/RangeMode ('near' or 'far') and log it; parse-only, no behaviour change for older firmware

v0.6:
	scan EVERY Bluetooth adapter (built-in and USB dongles), not just hci0; adapters that appear later are picked up too (field report: Cerbo GX with a USB Bluetooth adapter)

v0.5:
	wait for localsettings (and bluetoothd) at startup instead of failing per advert (Pi 4 boot race: "com.victronenergy.settings does not exist")
	restart our BLE discovery session every 60 s so readings keep updating when Venus 3.7x's own Bluetooth sensor scanner shares the adapter (values were frozen at the first reading on a Cerbo GX with two sensors)
	log a warning when no sensor advert has been heard for 3 minutes

v0.4:
	support advert v2 (firmware version byte + boost status bits); parse both v1 and v2
	(bytes 0-11 unchanged, v2 moves the checksum and appends a firmware-version byte)

v0.3:
	fix: executable bits on setup/run scripts (PackageManager refused v0.2 with "setup file not executable")

v0.2:
	SetupHelper / PackageManager packaging
	configuration moved to the GX UI (tank Setup page), persisted in localsettings
	out-of-the-box calibration defaults (empty 500 mm, full 50 mm) so a level shows immediately
	one private D-Bus connection per tank service (fixes registration, enables multiple sensors)
	config.json removed

v0.1:
	initial beta: passive BLE scan via BlueZ D-Bus, com.victronenergy.tank services, config.json calibration
